## protocol
## REAGENT SETUP
FGF basic $10\upmu\mathbf{g}\mathbf{m}\mathbf{l}^{-1}$ stock solution  Reconstitute the stock solution in PBS with $0.1\%$ wt/vol HSA. Aliquot and store at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 6 months.
Human ESC (hESC) medium  Combine $800\mathrm{ml}$ of DMEM/F12, $200\mathrm{ml}$ of KSR, $10\mathrm{ml}$ of MEM NEAA, $5\mathrm{ml}$ of $\mathbf{L}$ -glutamine and $1\mathrm{ml}$ of 2-mercapto­ethanol. Add FGF to a final concentration of $6\mathrm{{ng}\mathrm{{ml}^{-1}}}$ . Store at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 2 weeks.
$\mathbf{CaCl}_{2}$ solution  Mix $2.5\mathrm{M}\mathrm{CaCl}_{_2}$ solution with $\mathrm{ddH}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ . Filter-sterilize in a tissue culture hood and store at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
Coating buffer  To prepare coating buffer, mix $180\mathrm{ml}$ PBS, $20\mathrm{ml}$ of a $1\%$ (wt/vol) gelatin solution in PBS and $50\mathrm{ml}$ of poly l-lysine solution. Filter-sterilize in a tissue culture hood and store at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to a month.
HEPES-buffered saline, $2\times,\mathbf{pH}7.12$ Mix 28.1 ml of $5\mathrm{MNaCl}$ , $50\mathrm{ml}$ of 1 M HEPES, $5\mathrm{ml}$ of $150\mathrm{mM}$ ${\mathrm{Na}}_{_{2}}{\mathrm{HPO}}_{_{4}}$ and add $\mathrm{ddH}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ up to $500\mathrm{ml}$ . Titrate to $\mathrm{pH}7.12$ , if required, with $5\mathrm{MNaOH}$ . Filter-sterilize in a tissue culture hood, prepare aliquots of $10{-}20~\mathrm{ml}$ and store them at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to several months. Before use, mix well after thawing.
293T medium  To make 293T medium, add $50\mathrm{ml}$ of FBS, $5\mathrm{ml}$ of l-glutamine and $5\mathrm{ml}$ of $100\times$ penicillin-streptomycin in a ${500}\mathrm{-ml}$ bottle of DMEM. Store at $24^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 week.
MRC5 medium  To prepare MRC5 medium, add $50\mathrm{ml}$ of FBS to a ${500}\mathrm{-ml}$ bottle of EMEM. Store at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 month.
Gelatin-coated dishes  To prepare gelatin-coated dishes, add a sufficient volume of $0.1\%$ (wt/vol) gelatin solution to cover the bottom of the dish, incubate for at least $15\mathrm{min}$ at $24^{\circ}\mathrm{C},$ and aspirate off gelatin solution immediately before use. Do not store or allow plates to dry out.
Seeding dishes with MEFs  To seed dishes with MEF, thaw a vial of mitomycin C-treated MEFs and plate 10,000–12,000 cells per $\mathrm{cm}^{2}$ in the required number of gelatin-coated wells in six-well plates or $60\mathrm{-mm}$ dishes in DMEM with $10\%$ (vol/vol) FBS. Incubate at $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C},5\%$ $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ . Use within $16\mathrm{h}$ to $^\textrm{\scriptsize4d}$ after plating. Before use, wash out serum-containing medium with hESC medium.
Dispase solution  To prepare dispase solution, reconstitute lyophilized dispase to $6\mathrm{U}\mathrm{ml}^{-1}$ in hESC medium and filter-sterilize. Dispase solution can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for several weeks, but its activity may decrease with prolonged storage, and longer incubation times may be required for cell dissociation.
MEF-conditioned medium  To prepare MEF-conditioned medium (CM), plate mitotically inactive MEFs at 50,000 cells per $\mathrm{cm}^{2}$ in DMEM with $10\%$ (vol/vol) FBS in a $100\mathrm{-mm}$ dish. The next day, aspirate the medium, wash once with hESC medium and add $10~\mathrm{ml}$ hESC medium without FGF2. After $24\mathrm{h}$ , collect the CM and replace with new hESC medium. This can be repeated daily for up to 2 weeks. The CM can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 month. Supplement with $6\mathrm{ng}\mathrm{ml^{-1}}$ FGF2 before use.
Matrigel-coated plates  Slowly thaw Matrigel at $24^{\circ}\mathrm{C},$ immediately dilute 1:20 with DMEM/F12, and then transfer to plates (enough volume to cover the well surface). Incubate at $24^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^{\textrm{1h}}$ . Aspirate off the Matrigel ­solution immediately before plating the cells.  CRITICAL Matrigel will gelatinize at temperatures above $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . Thaw overnight at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ on ice, prepare $\scriptstyle1-\mathrm{ml}$ aliquots using precooled pipettes and tubes and store at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for several months.
Colony-PCR lysis buffer  Colony-PCR lysis buffer is prepared using $105\mathrm{mM}$ KCl, $14~\mathrm{mM}$ Tris-HCl, pH 8.3, 2.5 mM $\mathrm{{MgCl}_{2}};$ , $0.3~\mathrm{mg}\mathrm{ml^{-1}}$ gelatin, $0.45\%$ $\mathrm{(vol/vol)},$ ) NP-40, and $0.45\%$ (vol/vol) Tween 20. Prepare $_\mathrm{1-ml}$ aliquots and store at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for several months.
Oligonucleotides  Resuspend in WFI to prepare $100\upmu\mathrm{M}$ stock solutions.   
Store at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ long term or at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for several months.
Gag and human albumin probes for qPCR  Resuspend in WFI to prepare $100\upmu\mathrm{M}$ stock solutions. Store at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for several months.
hESC freezing medium $(2\times)$ hESC freezing medium is prepared using $60\%$ (vol/vol) FBS, $20\%$ (vol/vol) hESC medium and $20\%$ (vol/vol) DMSO. Prepare freshly for every use.
Depurination solution  Hydrochloric acid (HCl; $0.25\mathrm{N}$ ) is used as the depurination solution. It can be stored at room temperature (RT, $24^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ ) for several months.
