## B ox 2 | CRYOPRESERVATION OF CELLS
1. Aspirate medium and add $2~{\mathfrak{m}}!$ of dispase to one confluent $60\mathrm{-}\mathsf{m m}$ dish per iPSC line. Incubate at $37^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ for 6–7 min or until colonies detach.
2. Harvest colony fragments with a 2-ml serological pipette and transfer into a 15-ml conical tube. Add hESC medium up to $10~\mathrm{ml}$ and centrifuge at $320g$ for 5 min at $24^{\circ}\mathsf C$ .
3. Aspirate off supernatant, add $5~\mathsf{m l}$ of hESC medium and centrifuge at $320g$ for 5 min at $24^{\circ}\complement$ .
4. Aspirate off supernatant and resuspend in $1~{\mathfrak{m}}!$ of hESC medium.
5. Add $1~{\mathfrak{m}}!$ of $2\times$ freezing medium dropwise. Transfer $1~{\mathfrak{m}}!$ into each of two cryovials and place them in a freezing container and store overnight at $\mathtt{-80}^{\circ}\mathtt{C}$ . After $\mathsf{1}\mathsf{d}.$ , transfer the cryovials in a liquid $\mathsf{N}_{2}$ storage tank.
 PAUSE POINT Frozen cells can be stored indefinitely in liquid ${\sf N}_{2^{\prime}}$ if properly stored, but viability decreases with prolonged storage.
35| Discard the supernatant, leaving the pellet dry. Store at $\mathtt{-80}^{\circ}\mathtt{C}$ or proceed with extraction of genomic DNA.   
 PAUSE POINT Frozen cell pellets can be stored at $\mathtt{-80}^{\circ}\mathtt{C}$ for several months for DNA extraction at a later time.
36| DNA extraction: Extract genomic DNA using the DNeasy blood and tissue kit (or other equivalent kit) according to the manufacturer’s instructions. Resuspend in $100\upmu\upiota$ of WFI. Determine the DNA concentration using a spectrophotometer.
PAUSE POINT Genomic DNA can be stored at $\mathtt{-20}^{\circ}\mathtt{C}$ for several months.
37| Digestion of DNA: Digest $10\upmu\mathfrak{g}$ of genomic DNA from each PSC clone, as well as from untransduced PSCs as a negative control, with an appropriate restriction enzyme in a total volume of $50~\upmu\upiota$ for at least $16\mathrm{~h~}$ .
 PAUSE POINT Digested DNA can be stored at $4^{\circ}\complement$ for a few days or at $-20^{\circ}\complement$ for longer periods.
